  "notes": [
   "Inspired by Brew Dr. Clear Mind kombucha: a dry, peppery Saison with a restrained infusion of rosemary, peppermint, sage, and dandelion root. The herbs should complement the yeast rather than make the beer taste medicinal. HERB ADDITIONS AT FLAMEOUT: 0.08 oz (2.27 g) dried rosemary; 0.12 oz (3.40 g) dried peppermint; 0.04 oz (1.13 g) dried sage; 0.25 oz (7.09 g) roasted dandelion root. Turn off heat, add herbs in a fine mesh bag, steep 5 minutes, then remove and chill promptly. BeerXML compatibility note: the herb entries use USE=Boil and TIME=0 because FlameOut is not valid in strict BeerXML 1.0 and may be dropped by some importers. If the software displays the herbs as zero-minute boil additions, that is intentional. If a MISC quantity is not displayed after import, use the gram or ounce amounts in these notes. Ferment at 68 F for 24 hours, then allow to free-rise by roughly 2 F per day to 78 F. Hold until final gravity is stable. Carbonate to approximately 2.8 volumes CO2. Use culinary-quality dried herbs. Peppermint means dried peppermint leaf, not extract or oil."
  ],
